  "title": "Judean king who restored the temple",
  "era": "divided-kingdom",
  "lifespan": "c. 835–796 BC",
  "summary": "Joash became king of Judah at seven years old after being saved from Queen Athaliah's massacre of the royal family. Under the guidance of priest Jehoiada, he carried out a major restoration of the temple in Jerusalem. However, after Jehoiada's death, he turned away from the Lord and allowed the people to engage in idol worship, and was eventually killed by his own servants.",
